Negative control for the sort offer reading the module's own label channel
(`R6-6` · `R6-6b` · `R6-28`).

Removes the `i18n` PREFIX from the module's sort uischema. With no prefix,
`@jsonforms/core`'s `enumToEnumOptionMapper` falls back to `t(field, field)`, so
every option renders under its WIRE name (`default`, `created_at`) — the live
defect this channel replaced. The vocabulary is untouched: the same fields are
still offered and the status composite stays absent either way, which is the
half of `R6-6b` this must not be able to claim credit for.

Apply from the repo root: `git apply <this file>`; revert with `git apply -R`.

Reds: `runtime/components/__tests__/display-row.spec.ts` — the sort offer's
per-option assertion that every offered `label` is a catalogue value and no
option's `label` equals its own `value`.

